libfs: Fix duplicate directory entry in offset_dir_lookup

Backported fix for an issue where concurrent unlink operations during
directory listing could result in duplicate directory entries.

The root cause is in the offset_dir_lookup function, which uses mas_find
to determine the starting position for getdents calls. This can lead to
duplicate entries if a file is unlinked between calls. The fix replaces
mas_find with mas_find_rev to ensure the correct starting position.

This patch backports the fix to the older version of fs/libfs.c.